-- title:
--   Frobenius matrix on supersingular places equals the prime Hecke matrix
-- statement:
--   Let $q'$ be a prime and $\kappa$ an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q'$ that is algebraic over $\mathbb{Z}/q'$, and let $X_1$ be an elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\kappa$ with no nonzero $q'$-torsion point (every $P$ with $q'P=0$ vanishes). Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ satisfy `IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt`, i.e. $a<0$, $b<0$ and, for each height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$, the completion $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ is a division ring exactly when $q'\in v$. Let $\Lambda_1$ be a maximal order of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ (an order being a finitely generated $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule containing $1$, closed under multiplication and spanning the algebra over $\mathbb{Q}$, maximal among orders above it), and $\theta_1$ an injective ring homomorphism from the subring of $\mathrm{End}$ of $X_1$ generated by the rationally represented endomorphisms onto $\Lambda_1$. Let $N\ge 1$ with $q'\nmid N$, and let $m$ be a finite idele of the algebra with $m$ and $Nm^{-1}$ in the integral box $\widehat{\Lambda_1}=$ [`Submodule.finiteAdeleBox`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L14) $\Lambda_1$, with $\mathbb{H}\cap m\widehat{\Lambda_1}m^{-1}$ (`conjByFiniteIdele`) again a maximal order; put $R=\Lambda_1\cap(\mathbb{H}\cap m\widehat{\Lambda_1}m^{-1})$ and assume its relative index in $\Lambda_1$ as additive groups is $N$. Let $e$ be a bijection from the class set $\mathbb{H}^\times\backslash\widehat{\mathbb{H}}^\times/\,$`finiteIdeleStabilizer` $R$ onto the set of supersingular places of $\kappa(j(q),j(q^N))$ (rational affine geometric places whose value at the generator lies in the supersingular $j$-set for $q'$), subject to the hypothesis `he`: for every finite idele $x$, every elliptic $W$ and nonzero rationally represented $\chi\colon X_1\to W$, every $d\in\mathbb{H}^\times$ with $\theta_1(\mathrm{Hom}(W,X_1)\chi)=\overline{d\cdot\mathrm{ofFiniteIdele'}\ \Lambda_1\,x}$, and every elliptic $W'$ with rationally represented $\psi\colon W\to W'$, $\psi'\colon W'\to W$ satisfying $\psi'\psi=N=\psi\psi'$, such that $\theta_1$ carries the kernel ideal of $\psi\chi$ to $\overline{d\cdot\mathrm{ofFiniteIdele'}\ \Lambda_1\,(xm)}$ and $\ker\psi$ is cyclic of order $N$, the valuation subring of $e([x])$ is the pullback of that of the moduli place of $(W,\ker\psi)$ under the inclusion of $\kappa(j(q),j(q^N))$ into the full modular function field. Finally let `data` be a modular polynomial datum for $q'$ (monic $\Phi\in\mathbb{Z}[X][Y]$ of degree $\psi(q')$ annihilating $(j(q),j(q^{q'}))$) satisfying the Kronecker congruence $\Phi\equiv(Y^{q'}-X)(Y-X^{q'})\bmod q'$. Then for all classes $i,j$, the $(e\,i,e\,j)$ entry of `ssFrobMatrixC` — which is $1$ if the Frobenius map on geometric-level places sends $e\,j$ to $e\,i$ and $0$ otherwise — equals the $(i,j)$ entry of `classSetHeckeMatrix` for the stabiliser of $\widehat R$ and the set `primeHeckeSet` $R\,q'$ of ideles $h$ with $h,\,q'h^{-1}\in\widehat R$ and $h^{-1},\,q'^{-1}h\notin\widehat R$, namely the cardinality of the corresponding Hecke incidence set.
--
--   This is the Hecke clause of the Deuring–Eichler dictionary at the ramified prime $q'$: under a kernel-ideal adapted bijection between the class set of the Eichler order $R$ of level $N$ and the supersingular places of the level-$N$ modular function field in characteristic $q'$, the Frobenius permutation of supersingular places corresponds to right translation by the unique prime above $q'$, recorded as an equality of integer matrices. It is used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.exists_equiv_classSet_ssPlaces_degeneracy_hecke_comm`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.exists_equiv_classSet_ssPlaces_degeneracy_hecke_comm), which packages the bijection together with its compatibility with the degeneracy and Hecke structures.
